@startuml
' Where the authored metadata lives.
'
' One polymorphic table, so the package works with any model without knowing
' anything about it. Rows are created lazily: a record that has never been
' given metadata has no row, and behaves exactly as it did before.

title Storage

skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #ffffff
  BorderColor #475569
  ArrowColor #475569
}
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class "seos" <<table>> {
  --
  + id : bigint
  + seoable_type : string
  + seoable_id : bigint
  + title : string?
  + description : text?
  + image_url : string(2048)?
  + image_alt : string?
  + canonical_url : string(2048)?
  + robots : string
  + type : string
  + created_at, updated_at
}

class "Seo" <<model>> {
  --
  + toSeoData() : SeoData
  + seoable() : MorphTo
}

class "Product" <<your model>> {
  --
  + seo() : MorphOne
  + getSeoData() : SeoData
  + getSeoRecord() : Seo?
  + saveSeo(array) : Seo
}

class "Article" <<your model>> {
  --
  + seo() : MorphOne
}

class "HasSeo" <<interface>>

class "InteractsWithSeo" <<trait>>

note right of seos
  __robots__ defaults to
  "index, follow" and __type__
  to "website", so a row is
  never non-indexable by
  accident.

  Both are NOT NULL; the
  package treats them as
  always present.
end note

note bottom of seos
  __One row per describable record.__
  A record with no row is not an error:
  the model falls back to values
  generated from its own attributes.
end note

Seo ..> seos : maps to
InteractsWithSeo ..|> HasSeo : implements
Product ..> InteractsWithSeo : use
Product ..|> HasSeo : implements
Article ..> InteractsWithSeo : use
Seo "1" <-- "0..1" Product : seoable_id
Seo "1" <-- "0..1" Article : seoable_id

@enduml
